if ڕ else
Many times, you will want to do one thing if a value is true and another if it is false. At
these times, you must add an else clause to the if statement:
bool night = false;
if (night) {
print( "It's night." );
} else {
print( "It's daytime. Why don't you go outside and enjoy yourself?" );
}
// The output of this code will be:
// It's daytime. Why don't you go outside and enjoy yourself?
In this case, because night is false, the code in the else clause is executed.
